results.description:
a habit tracker for developers and minimalists, built for iPhone and styled like the command line you live in.
// quiet. opinionated. monospaced.

$ cat features.txt

[*] five tracking modes — checkbox, counter, number, health, time
[*] routines — group habits into morning, workout, evening, anything
[*] streaks with shields — protect a 75 hard run, or any streak, from one bad day
[*] a github-style contribution graph — your whole history, filling in pixel by pixel
[*] smart reminders — per habit or one for a whole routine; useful pings, not ten-a-day spam
[*] focus timer with pomodoro — Live Activity on the lock screen, Dynamic Island when running
[*] Apple Watch app — check habits off on your wrist, run a timer, 25 complications for your watch face
[*] Siri and Shortcuts — check off a habit or a whole routine by voice, start a timer, ask what is left today; 16 actions for your own automations
[*] Spotlight — your habits and routines in iPhone search, by their own name or by the routine they belong to
[*] in your browser too — the whole tracker at app.inithabits.com, nothing to install
[*] cloud sync — iPhone, watch and browser updating each other in real time; sign in with Apple, Google or email
[*] achievements, xp and levels — progress that adds up, without the noise
[*] vacation mode — freeze your streaks while you are away, come back to them intact
[*] 23 themes + a custom theme editor — tokyo night, dracula, catppuccin, and more
[*] iCloud sync — your data, your iCloud, your control
[*] Apple Health auto-sync — steps, sleep, water, mindful minutes, medication doses
[*] nine widgets — checklist, heatmap, contribution grid, ring, quick icons, next up, week view, mood
[*] backup and export — an iCloud backup, or a json file that is yours to keep
[*] fifteen languages — english, dutch, german, spanish, french, italian, portuguese, russian, ukrainian, polish, turkish, czech, japanese, chinese, korean
[*] local-first — works fully offline, no sign-up or account needed
[*] privacy — passcode, biometric lock, app-switcher blur, lock-screen redaction
[*] no ads, no AI, no dark patterns

$ cat philosophy.txt

// built solo over hundreds of testing hours.
// no analytics that track who you are.
// no algorithm trying to maximise your screen time.
// shipping new features frequently.

$ cat pro.txt

// the core experience is free: 10 habits, 2 routines, three manual tracking modes,
// eight built-in themes, the checklist widget, the watch app with three complications,
// cloud sync across iPhone, watch and browser, and local storage.

// pro raises limits and unlocks: timer + healthkit modes, all 23 themes,
// custom theme editor, seven extra fonts, iCloud sync, the other eight widgets,
// 22 more complications, passcode + biometric lock, Live Activity timer.

// pro is monthly, annual (with 7-day trial), or lifetime — one-time, no expiration.

> thank you for supporting a solo dev.
